    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: fiscal-year basis for date-derived values\n\nThe fiscal year starts **1 July** and is labelled by the calendar year it ends in (e.g. 2 Jul 2025 \u2192 `FY26`, 30 Jun 2026 \u2192 `FY26`).\n\n**New file \u2014 `util/FiscalYears.java`**: the single source of the fiscal-year rule.\n- `fiscalYearOf(date)` \u2192 full fiscal year (`year + 1` from July onward, else `year`)\n- `yearSegment(date)` \u2192 zero-padded last two digits (`\"26\"`)\n- `labelFor(owner)` \u2192 `\"FY<YY>\"` from the owner's registrationDate, or `null` when absent (mirroring how `ageBand` is absent).\n\n**`fiscalYear` response field** (`FY<YY>`):\n- Added to the `OwnerDto` schema in `openapi.yml` (readOnly string), so the generated DTO gets the field.\n- Wired in `OwnerMapper` via an expression mapping to `FiscalYears.labelFor(owner)`.\n\n**Membership identifier year segment** (`AssignMembershipNumber`): `<customerCode>-M<YY>` now uses the fiscal-year `yearSegment` of the business-day-adjusted registration date instead of the raw calendar year. (Verified: reg 2026-08-11 \u2192 `...-M27`, matching `FY27`.)\n\n**Tenure** (`MembershipLevels`): the +3 points rule now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearOf(today) \u2212 fiscalYearOf(registrationDate)`) and awards points for tenure over one fiscal year, replacing the old 365-day window. A newly-created owner still scores 0 tenure.\n\nDocs (javadoc + the two OpenAPI descriptions for `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints`) were updated to describe the fiscal-year basis.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
